D03 -- THE DUST-LAW INVERSION: c_dust(M500, r) as a total-mass estimator
============================================================================================

============================================================================================
PART 1 -- THE INVERSION: the closed form and the floor propagation
============================================================================================
  the committed law (G143): c_dust = 0.72 (M500/8e14)^q (r/R500)^p
    c0 = -0.1427 (log10 0.72), q = -0.4144 (derived -0.3333), p = -0.990
    residual floor: 0.119 dex (3-param) / 0.097 dex (13-param)
  THE INVERSION: log10(M/8e14) = (log10 c_dust - c0 - p log10(r/R500))/q
    -> sigma(log10 M) = sigma(log10 c_dust)/|q|
  [q_measured] sigma_M = 0.287 dex (0.119 floor) / 0.234 dex (0.097 floor); two-radius /sqrt2: 0.203 / 0.166 dex
  [q_derived_-1/3] sigma_M = 0.357 dex (0.119 floor) / 0.291 dex (0.097 floor); two-radius /sqrt2: 0.252 / 0.206 dex
  [PASS] P1a [the inversion closed form, arithmetic] two radii with the law exact return the same M (consistency by construction)
        measured: single-radius formula applied to a synthetic law field: |d log10 M| = 0.0 exactly
        reading : two equations, one unknown: the estimator is the log-space mean of the two single-radius estimates; their spread is the radial-shape consistency diagnostic

  synthetic round-trip (4 cases): |delta log10 M| < 1e-9 -- EXACT
  [PASS] P1b [the two-radii estimator] the combined estimator and its internal consistency diagnostic
        measured: M_dust-inv = 8e14 x 10^mean(log10 M(r1), log10 M(r2)); the |spread| of the two single-radius values is the radial-shape residual of that cluster (measured on X-COP below)
        reading : the estimator returns one mass per cluster from the two-radius field; the per-cluster two-radius spread must sit at or below the propagated floor for the law to be self-similar in r (it is the 0.097-dex one-shape statement from the other side)


  [PASS] P1v [V1: the inversion's precision] the residual floor propagates through |q| into the mass
        measured: sigma_M = 0.119/|q| = 0.287 dex (committed q); 0.097/|q| = 0.234 dex; derived q=-1/3: 0.357 / 0.291 dex
        reading : the dust-law M estimator's honest single-field precision is the 0.23-0.29-dex class at the committed q; the derived q=-1/3 carries 0.29-0.36 dex (the 0.52-sigma q shift costs the factor 3/2.414 in the propagator)


